Ze patch to the Go standard library: crypto/tls chooses a server session_id.

How this file is applied, reviewed and replaced on a Go upgrade:
docs/contributing/patching-the-standard-library.md

RFC 5216 Section 2.1.1: "If the peer's sessionId is null or unrecognized by
the server, the server MUST choose the sessionId to establish a new session."
crypto/tls sends an empty session_id on every TLS 1.2 full handshake. The hunk
below makes a full handshake that issues no session ticket send a fresh
32-octet session_id; a handshake that issues a ticket keeps the empty id
(RFC 5077 Section 3.4). The added file declares the marker constant that Ze's
EAP-TLS authenticator references, so an unpatched build does not compile.

The stamp names the Go release whose doFullHandshake was read against this
hunk. A toolchain of any other version refuses until the function is re-read
and the stamp changed (page section "When the Go version changes").

Ze-Reviewed-Against: go1.27.3

diff --git a/src/crypto/tls/handshake_server.go b/src/crypto/tls/handshake_server.go
index a05d6c896b..f800241efd 100644
--- a/src/crypto/tls/handshake_server.go
+++ b/src/crypto/tls/handshake_server.go
@@ -600,6 +600,19 @@ func (hs *serverHandshakeState) doFullHandshake() error {
 	}
 
 	hs.hello.ticketSupported = hs.clientHello.ticketSupported && !c.config.SessionTicketsDisabled
+	// Ze patch, docs/contributing/patching-the-standard-library.md.
+	// RFC 5216 Section 2.1.1: "If the peer's sessionId is null or
+	// unrecognized by the server, the server MUST choose the sessionId to
+	// establish a new session." A full handshake that issues no ticket
+	// names its session with a fresh 32-octet id (RFC 5246 Section 7.4.1.2,
+	// SessionID<0..32>); one that issues a ticket keeps the empty id
+	// (RFC 5077 Section 3.4).
+	if !hs.hello.ticketSupported {
+		hs.hello.sessionId = make([]byte, 32)
+		if _, err := io.ReadFull(c.config.rand(), hs.hello.sessionId); err != nil {
+			return err
+		}
+	}
 	hs.hello.cipherSuite = hs.suite.id
 
 	hs.finishedHash = newFinishedHash(hs.c.vers, hs.suite)
diff --git a/src/crypto/tls/zz_ze_server_session_id.go b/src/crypto/tls/zz_ze_server_session_id.go
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..4b0e31bda2
--- /dev/null
+++ b/src/crypto/tls/zz_ze_server_session_id.go
@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+// Ze patch, docs/contributing/patching-the-standard-library.md.
+
+package tls
+
+// ZeServerChoosesSessionID marks a crypto/tls carrying Ze's server session_id
+// patch: a TLS 1.2 full handshake that issues no session ticket sends a fresh
+// 32-octet session_id. RFC 5216 Section 2.1.1: "If the peer's sessionId is
+// null or unrecognized by the server, the server MUST choose the sessionId to
+// establish a new session." Ze's EAP-TLS authenticator references this
+// constant, so it does not compile against an unpatched GOROOT.
+const ZeServerChoosesSessionID = true
